  "id": "fatty-acid-amide-hydrolase",
  "term": "fatty acid amide hydrolase",
  "definition": "Fatty acid amide hydrolase (FAAH) is an enzyme that mainly breaks down the endocannabinoid anandamide and related fatty acid amides, helping end their effects. By controlling this breakdown, it helps regulate endocannabinoid signaling and can influence processes linked to behavior, such as mood, cognition, pain, appetite, and addiction.",
